    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n11348" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπᾰμείβομαι</span></b> , fut.
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ψομαι</span>: aor.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπημείφθην</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					X.
					<u>An.</u>
					2.5.15
				</span></i>
			: plpf.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπάμειπτο</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>AP</u>
					14.2
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Nonn.
				<u>D.</u>
				8.165
			</span></i>:—<i>reply, answer,</i> freq. in <i><span class="en">
				Hom.
			</span></i>, but always with a second more definite Verb, as 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπαμειβόμενος προσέφη</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					1.84
				</span></i>
			, al.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπαμείβετς φώνησέν τε</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					20.199
				</span></i>
			, al.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὧδε ἀ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					X.
				</span></i>
			 l.c.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τινά</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Theoc.
					8.8
				</span></i>
			.</div>
